  "instance_name": "false_equivalence",
  "label": "False Equivalence",
  "description": "A logical fallacy that occurs when two things are presented as being equivalent when they are not. The meme uses this fallacy to equate the inability to properly vet Syrian migrants with the need to disarm 'safest demographics' in Canada. This requires knowledge of logical fallacies and their use in propaganda, which is not visible in the image but is essential to understand the meme's flawed reasoning.",
